preConditionHook:
// THE ORIGINAL CHESTER KELTNER CHANNEL (G16-23, the glossary entry and the one
// place Grimes states the indicator before the modern ATR modification): a
// simple average of the TYPICAL PRICE (high + low + close) / 3, offset by a
// multiple of the average bar RANGE. Long when the close is above the upper
// channel, short when below the lower one -- a STATE, not a cross.
//
// Not KeltnerChannelCross and not the EMA/ATR Keltner band rules in this slice,
// on three differences at once: the centre series is the typical price rather
// than the close or an EMA, the band series is the MEAN BAR RANGE rather
// than an ATR, and the test is a state rather than EL's `crosses` state
// machine. Range averaging ignores gaps where True Range folds them in, which
// is the whole behavioural difference from the corpus's ATR bands. bandMult is
// unspecified by the book; 1.0 chosen, 10 / 10 are Keltner's own lengths.
//
// EL's Average RECOMPUTES FROM SCRATCH every bar (VERIFIED, 2,808/2,808 bars),
// so these are FRESH loops over price -- not the WFSafe_AvgTrueRange rolling
// accumulator and not a mirrored variable buffer, because both series are
// expressions over PRICE, which has real history. Summed newest-first, EL's
// Summation order, and the / 3 is applied per term exactly as EL evaluates the
// expression bar by bar before summing it.
// Scratch is declared in localVariables, not at hook scope: the generator only
// prefixes declared locals, so a hook-scope declaration is a redefinition when
// this rule is placed twice in one strategy.
tpAvg = 0.0;
for (int i = 0; i < (int)maLength; ++i) {
    tpAvg += (high[i] + low[i] + close[i]) / 3.0;
}
tpAvg /= (int)maLength;
rangeAvg = 0.0;
for (int i = 0; i < (int)rangeLength; ++i) {
    rangeAvg += high[i] - low[i];
}
rangeAvg /= (int)rangeLength;
